<Layout title="About — Letters Home">
  <div class="about-page">
    <h1>About This Project</h1>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>The Story</h2>
      <p>
        In 1968, two brothers from Decatur, Illinois served simultaneously in Vietnam.
        Mike Ducy served aboard USS Jouett (DLG-29), a guided missile frigate on search
        and rescue duty in the Gulf of Tonkin. His younger brother Bill served as a Marine,
        on the ground in Da Nang and Hoi An.
      </p>
      <p>
        They wrote letters home. They recorded cassette tapes. Mike kept a daily logbook
        and shot Super 8 film of helicopter rescues, port calls, and life at sea. Back in
        Decatur, their parents followed the war through their sons' words and the evening news.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site presents their story day by day, from the primary sources they left behind.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>The Archives</h2>
      <p>
        The material on this site comes from the personal archives of FTG3 Michael F. Ducy, USN,
        preserved by his family for almost 60 years. The collection includes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>44 handwritten and typewritten letters from Mike (August 1967 &ndash; October 1968)</li>
        <li>17 letters from PFC Bill Ducy, USMC (May 1968 &ndash; October 1969)</li>
        <li>11 familygrams from Captain Robert S. Hayes to crew families</li>
        <li>A 187-page daily logbook covering the entire deployment</li>
        <li>24 cassette tape recordings between the brothers and family</li>
        <li>Super 8 film footage of SAR operations, port calls, and homecoming</li>
        <li>109 photographs from Decatur to the Gulf of Tonkin</li>
        <li>Ship publications, newspaper clippings, and service records</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Credits</h2>
      <p>
        Digitized and curated by Michael Ducy II.
      </p>
      <p>
        Logbook pages, letters, and documents transcribed using Claude AI vision
        from scanned originals. Audio recordings denoised and transcribed using
        OpenAI's Whisper. Please contact <a href="mailto:vietnam@ducy.org">vietnam@ducy.org</a> 
        if you find errors.
      </p>
      <p>
        Thank you to the following for their contributions to this project:
        <ul>
